Case Study – Fake Investment Fraud

Scenario

Customer was convinced to invest in a fake high-return investment scheme.

The fraudster instructed the customer to keep the investment confidential and not disclose the purpose of the transactions to bank staff or anyone else.

Believing the investment was genuine, the customer proceeded with the transactions through the branch.


Transaction Summary

Customer transferred a total of SAR 455,000 through the branch.

A total of 3 transactions were performed.

The transactions comprised 1 internal transfer and 2 RTGS transfers.


Outcome

The customer incurred a financial loss of SAR 455,000 after the funds were transferred to accounts controlled by the fraudster under a Fake Investment scam.
The customer was assured that the investment would generate high returns within a short period.
